comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:34:56.161Z","harness:claude-code","Measured 2026-07-29: the placeholder block has a lifecycle consequence that was not previously recorded. Sixteen closed items carry no close_reason and validate warns on all of them, and every one of those sixteen carries the placeholder resolution sentence Resolution normalized from closed status because the field was missing or low-signal, plus the matching actual_result placeholder. Two further items in the same warning set - pm-7vm9 and pm-qa2h - carry real recorded resolutions describing what actually shipped, and their close_reason was backfilled honestly from that record today, dropping the count from 18 to 16. The split is exact: where a real resolution exists the missing close_reason is recoverable from the tracker itself, and where the placeholder sentence sits there the record contains nothing to recover from. The normalization sweep that wrote those sentences therefore did more than add noise to relevance scoring - it consumed the only field that could have told a later reader whether the closure evidence was ever captured, and it did so in a way that is indistinguishable from a genuine one-line resolution to every consumer except a literal string match. Any future normalization must write a value that is machine-distinguishable from an authored one."
  "2026-10-02T18:38:05.708Z","harness:codex","Current evidence 2026-10-02: validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift reads all 2863 records with zero missing/unreadable streams, hash/chain/version/workspace-state mismatches or drift. It checks 2551 closed items and warns on 170 missing structured resolution fields. This extends the existing historical evidence-quality census; the two current delivery closures contain explicit resolution, expected and actual values. No placeholder backfill or guessed historical claim was written. This owner remains open and unclaimed for evidence-derived cleanup, and passing integrity is not represented as complete historical resolution metadata."
  "2026-10-06T11:54:16.103Z","harness:codex","Current evidence 2026-10-06: full validation reads 2898 records with zero history drift, storage duplicates, unreadable streams, hash/chain/version mismatches or workspace-state drift. It checks 2583 closed items and still warns on the same 170 historical missing structured resolution fields. The three new delivery closures have explicit resolution, expected and actual values in their immutable close events. This updates the existing census; no placeholder backfill, duplicate cleanup item or guessed historical observation is introduced. Integrity admission passes separately from this outstanding metadata-quality warning."
  "2026-10-28T08:54:42.340Z","harness:codex","PR #1616 review revalidated the canonical placeholder residual: all 16 full live records and their complete histories still have empty close_reason and the identical low-signal normalization resolution/expected/actual markers; none contains a substantive close_reason event. IDs: pm-mve5, pm-sgko, pm-h2pi, pm-daft, pm-wvhs, pm-slul, pm-l9j6, pm-hiji, pm-7k9o, pm-5na9, pm-32si, pm-2lbp, pm-k213, pm-f9s0, pm-dqer, pm-6js7. This existing open owner explicitly retains their evidence-recovery work. The count is 16, not zero; do not copy a placeholder into close_reason. The completed pm-e9zh 622-field bounded recovery and its separate 170 missing-structured-field residual remain accurately distinguished. No affected historical item or closure attribution was rewritten."
  "2026-10-30T00:00:30.371Z","harness:codex","2026-10-29 strict complete-corpus refresh: the same16 pre-existing closed rows still lack close_reason; all seven current delivery closures have explicit reasons and structured evidence. The separate170 missing structured-field residual remains the documented bounded-backfill result. Current3162-item history validation reports zero drift and identity discontinuities. Retain this existing placeholder-recovery owner open and unclaimed; no duplicate cleanup item or placeholder field fill was introduced."
